  <h1>The Death Sentence That Became a Daily Pill: How HIV Got Managed</h1>
  <p class="dek">In 1995 a positive test was a death sentence. One man counted a billion viruses a day. Disease with no cure became a daily pill. 32 million people take it.</p>
